#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Launch a lead's worker into its WORKER box (or LEAD or OTHER box), and archive a box safely.

  ade-worker-run --lead ID --slice NAME [--window-middle WORK] [--repo NAME] [--cwd DIR] [--worktree DIR] [--no-footer]
                 [--placement worker|lead|other | --interactive | --other] -- <paseo run args...>
  ade-worker-run archive-window --lead ID [--window-middle WORK] [--repo NAME] [--placement worker|other] [--idle-handled] [--dry-run]
  ade-worker-run rename-main --lead ID [--window-middle WORK] [--repo NAME]      (alias: rename-lead)
  (launch and archive-window take --on-behalf-of-lead: needed when $PASEO_AGENT_ID is set and is not --lead)

Three boxes per lead and repo (operator ruling 2026-11-14, docs/workspace-layout.md): `LEAD <repo> (<work>)` is the lead's own
window (the tab row that includes the lead), `WORKER <repo> (<work>)` holds every worker and reviewer the lead starts,
`OTHER <repo> (<work>)` holds probes and side tasks. A name is `<KIND> <repo> (<work>)` (bin/ade_ws_names.py); the lead id is
NOT in it (it stays in the tab name and the ade.lead label). The 2026-11-13 kinds MAIN, WORKERS and USER are still found
(as LEAD, WORKER, OTHER) and renamed to the current kind when a launch reuses the window. <repo> is --repo, else the repo of
--cwd (the main checkout's name, also from a linked worktree). rename-lead never takes the home directory's name as a repo (a window
whose cwd is $HOME needs --repo, or a bare `LEAD <repo>` name that already says it), and with --repo or --window-middle it corrects a
window already named in the current form (a launch never does).

Launch (default --placement worker): ONE box per lead and repo, whatever the slice and whatever --window-middle says: the lead's
box is found by ownership (never by its name) and reused. A successor lead of a completed self-handoff (bin/ade_lead_succession.py)
reuses the box its predecessors made. Ownership is evidence: the lead's window record ($ADE_WORKER_RUN_STATE/<lead id>.windows.json),
a live agent labelled ade.lead=<lead or a predecessor> in it, or the lead id in a legacy name (`workers <middle> <lead id>`, renamed
first). Refused: a window registered to another lead or holding an agent labelled for another lead; adopting a window that holds
agents not labelled for this lead; several owned boxes of the repo with no --window-middle (or none naming one) to pick one. A box
of ANOTHER repo is not this launch's: the launch opens its own (`--new-workspace local`, in --cwd's primary checkout, never a claimed
worktree), reads the new window's id from the launch (JSON `workspaceId`, else the `Created workspace wks_... - <name>` stderr line,
cross-checked against the agent's state file) and names it `WORKER <repo> (<work>)`.
--window-middle is only the `(<work>)` text of a box this launch opens (default `workers`; `other` in the OTHER box), and, when the
lead owns several boxes of the repo, picks the one with that text. It never opens a second box. Old invocations keep working.
--placement other (alias --other): the same for the OTHER box; label ade.placement=other, tab `other <slice> <lead id>`.
--placement lead (aliases main, --interactive; for a worker the OPERATOR asked for interactively): launches into the lead's own
window, resolved from the lead's agent record ($PASEO_AGENT_ID must be --lead); it must be named `LEAD <repo> (<work>)` (a MAIN name
is renamed to that) or the launch is refused (`rename-main` fixes that); never archived by this tool. Label ade.placement=main.
Tab names: `worker <slice> <lead id>` plus ` [wt: <worktree dir>]` when --worktree DIR names the worktree the worker writes in or
--cwd is a linked worktree (a hint, shortened to fit 100 characters; the brief still carries the path). Every launch carries
`--label ade.lead=<lead>` and `--label slice=<NAME>`. One JSON line goes to stdout: {agentId, workspaceId, windowName, tabName}
(plus reportPath and donePath unless --no-footer).
Pass --no-wait to paseo. The last `--` argument (the brief) gets one line appended: `Also follow every item of <repo root>/docs/
dispatch-footer.md.` (skipped by --no-footer; refused when the last argument is not recognisably the brief). A `Footer values:` line
always follows it and fills {lead}, {report}, {done}, {inbox} and {replies}. A report path the brief LABELS (a line-start `Report:`/
`Report path:`/`Report file:` with the path on that line or the next (one blank line allowed), a `## Report path` heading with the
path below, "write|save your report [file] to|at|in|as <path>", `{report} = <path>`) is used as {report} and nothing is generated or
created; {done} is the brief's labelled `Done marker:`/`Done file:`/`Done path:`/`{done} =` path (ignored when that file exists; a bare
`Done:` is no label), else `<report>.done`. A `>` quoted line labels nothing, and two different labelled report paths (or done markers)
are refused rather than picked by position. A path merely mentioned (an input report of another agent) is not a label; when no label
matches and the brief names a `-report.md` or `agent-reports/` path, a stderr warning names it and the generated one. A generated stub
is removed again only when `paseo run` exits nonzero (no agent exists) and the file is still the exact stub this launch created. Otherwise report = ~/.local/state/agent-reports/<lead id>/
<slice>-report.md (or $AGENT_FOOTER_REPORT_DIR/<lead id>/..., the agent_footer_gate layout; `worker-` is prefixed to a slice starting with
report/summary/findings/analysis, whose .md Claude Code refuses to Write), done = <report>.done, and a report or .done that exists is
never reused: the next free `<slice>-N-report.md` is taken. A generated report is created exclusively (`STATUS: working`) in a 700
directory just before the launch. The chosen paths go to stderr and the JSON (reportPath, donePath), so the lead can wait on the .done.
A box a launch opens is created in --cwd's primary checkout: the launch is refused unless the brief names --cwd by absolute path, and
the JSON line then carries cwd and requestedCwd. --cwd must be the directory of the box the worker is placed in (`paseo run
--workspace` ignores it, getpaseo/paseo#9699): a different --cwd is refused before anything is renamed or launched, and after every
launch with --cwd the agent's Cwd is read back and a mismatch stops the fresh worker (an interrupt, not an archive).
Strips PASEO_AGENT_ID, PASEO_AGENT_CWD and PASEO_WORKSPACE_ID from every paseo call.

archive-window: `paseo workspace archive` of the lead's WORKER (or OTHER) box only when the preconditions of docs/workspace-layout.md
hold (every live agent labelled ade.lead=<lead> in that window is closed, or idle with --idle-handled; no other live agent in the
window; the window is this lead's box); otherwise it lists the blockers and archives nothing. A LEAD window is never archived; only
the matched window's own agents block it (an agent of the lead in the LEAD window, the OTHER box or a second WORKER window never does). `ade-tidy --apply` archives the extra windows a chain left.

Exit 0: done; 1: refused or paseo failed (message on stderr; an agent already launched is named); 2: usage.
See docs/workspace-layout.md and skills/fan-out section 3.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import fcntl
import functools
import json
import os
from pathlib import Path
import re
import shlex
import stat
import subprocess
import sys
import tempfile
import unicodedata
from typing import NamedTuple

import ade_claims
import ade_mcp_on_demand as mcpod
import ade_lead_succession as succ  # bin/ is sys.path[0] for a script run by path or through a symlink
import ade_ws_names as wsn

ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
FOOTER = ROOT / "docs/dispatch-footer.md"
# `paseo run` flags that take a value, and boolean ones: the brief is the last argument only when what precedes it shows so.
VALUE_FLAGS = ("--provider", "--model", "-m", "--mode", "--title", "--thinking", "--label", "--image", "--wait-timeout", "--base",
               "--branch", "--new-branch", "--worktree-mode", "--worktree-slug", "--pr-number", "--forge", "--env", "-e",
               "--name", "--effort", "--system-prompt", "--timeout", "--output-schema")
BOOL_FLAGS = ("--no-wait", "--json")  # `paseo run` has no -d/--detach/--background of its own
STRIP = ("PASEO_AGENT_ID", "PASEO_AGENT_CWD", "PASEO_WORKSPACE_ID")
LEAD_RE = re.compile(r"[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}")
SLICE_RE = re.compile(r"[A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*")
WKS_RE = re.compile(r"wks_[A-Za-z0-9]+")
CREATED_RE = re.compile(r"^Created workspace (wks_[A-Za-z0-9]+) - ", re.M)
NAME_LIMIT = wsn.NAME_LIMIT
CLI_TIMEOUT = 60
# Flags the helper owns; a caller passing one would break the placement or the labels.
OWNED_FLAGS = ("--workspace", "--new-workspace", "--cwd", "--dir", "-C", "--host", "--home", "-o", "--format", "-q", "--quiet")
DETACH_FLAGS = ("--no-wait", "-d", "--background", "--detach")
OWNED_LABEL_KEYS = ("ade.lead", "slice", "ade.placement")
DEFAULT_WORK = {"WORKER": "workers", "OTHER": "other"}  # the (<work>) text of a box opened without --window-middle


class Refused(Exception):
    pass


def child_env() -> dict[str, str]:
    return {k: v for k, v in os.environ.items() if k not in STRIP}


def paseo(args: list[str], timeout: int | None = CLI_TIMEOUT) -> tuple[int, str, str]:
    """One paseo call, argv list, stdout and stderr read back from files (never a pipe)."""
    with tempfile.TemporaryFile("w+") as out, tempfile.TemporaryFile("w+") as err:
        try:
            rc = subprocess.run(["paseo", *args], env=child_env(), stdin=subprocess.DEVNULL, stdout=out,
                                stderr=err, timeout=timeout).returncode
        except FileNotFoundError:
            raise Refused("paseo is not on PATH")
        except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
            raise Refused(f"paseo {' '.join(args[:2])} timed out after {timeout}s")
        out.seek(0)
        err.seek(0)
        return rc, out.read(), err.read()


def paseo_json(args: list[str]):
    rc, out, err = paseo(args)
    if rc != 0:
        raise Refused(f"paseo {' '.join(args[:2])} failed (rc {rc}): {err.strip() or out.strip()}")
    try:
        return json.loads(out)
    except ValueError:
        raise Refused(f"paseo {' '.join(args[:2])} did not print JSON")


def build_name(kind: str, repo: str, work: str) -> str:
    try:
        return wsn.build(kind, repo, work)
    except ValueError as e:
        raise Refused(str(e))


def check_names(lead: str, slice_name: str | None) -> None:
    if not LEAD_RE.fullmatch(lead):
        raise Refused("--lead must be the lead's full agent id (a lowercase UUID)")
    if slice_name is not None:
        if not SLICE_RE.fullmatch(slice_name):
            raise Refused("--slice must match [A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._-]*")
        for box in wsn.TAB_PREFIX:  # the longest tab prefix decides; the ` [wt: ...]` part shortens itself
            if len(wsn.tab_name(box, slice_name, lead)) > NAME_LIMIT:
                raise Refused(f"tab name `{wsn.tab_name(box, slice_name, lead)}` exceeds {NAME_LIMIT} characters")


def list_windows() -> list[dict]:
    rows = paseo_json(["workspace", "ls", "--json"])
    if not isinstance(rows, list):
        raise Refused("paseo workspace ls --json did not return a list")
    return [r for r in rows if isinstance(r, dict) and isinstance(r.get("name"), str)]


def predecessor_acting(pred: str) -> str | None:
    """Why `pred` (an agent that handed off to the lead but is not archived yet) may still be acting, None when it is not:
    `paseo agent inspect --json` reads Archived true, or Archived false with Status idle or closed. Anything else (running,
    another status, an unreadable or mismatched answer, a failed inspect) is a reason: fail closed (hf-38c)."""
    try:
        rc, out, err = paseo(["agent", "inspect", pred, "--json"])
    except Refused as e:
        return f"its state cannot be read ({e})"
    if rc != 0:
        return f"its state cannot be read (paseo agent inspect exited {rc})"
    try:
        data = json.loads(out)
    except ValueError:
        return "its state cannot be read (paseo agent inspect did not print JSON)"
    if not isinstance(data, dict) or data.get("Id") != pred or not isinstance(data.get("Archived"), bool):
        return "its state cannot be read (unexpected paseo agent inspect answer)"
    if data["Archived"]:
        return None
    status = data.get("Status")
    pending = data.get("PendingPermissions")  # `finish`'s own idle test needs [] too (ade_self_session.py): a card open means it may still act
    if status in ("idle", "closed") and pending == []:
        return None
    if status in ("idle", "closed"):
        return f"it has pending permission requests or an unreadable permission list ({pending!r:.60})"
    return f"it is not archived and its status is {status!r}"


@functools.lru_cache(maxsize=None)  # one reading per process: a launch decides and explains from the same inspect
def ack_adoption(lead: str) -> tuple[set[str], dict[str, str]]:
    """(ids adopted, {predecessor: reason not adopted}) for the fresh acknowledged self-handoffs that name THIS lead as successor
    (ade_lead_succession.acknowledged_predecessors; a stale record or one naming another agent is no link). An adopted predecessor
    is one that is no longer acting (predecessor_acting) and brings its own completed chain; the rest stay foreign (hf-38c)."""
    adopted: set[str] = set()
    blocked: dict[str, str] = {}
    for pred in succ.acknowledged_predecessors(lead):
        why = predecessor_acting(pred)
        if why is not None:
            blocked[pred] = why
            continue
        try:
            chain_ids = succ.lineage(pred)
        except succ.SuccessionError as e:
            raise Refused(f"{e}; fix or remove the handoff records in {succ.default_state_dir()} by hand")
        if lead in chain_ids:
            raise Refused(f"lead succession from {pred} reaches {lead} again: the ledger is cyclic")
        adopted |= chain_ids
    return adopted, blocked


def lineage(lead: str) -> set[str]:
    """`lead` plus the archived leads it replaced through completed self-handoffs (bin/ade_lead_succession.py), plus the
    predecessors of a fresh acknowledged self-handoff that have stopped acting (ack_adoption). Their window
    records and `ade.lead` labels are this lead's: an acknowledged handoff must not strand the predecessor's windows and
    workers (2026-11-14). A cyclic ledger is refused loudly, never read as "no predecessors"."""
    try:
        base = succ.lineage(lead)
    except succ.SuccessionError as e:
        raise Refused(f"{e}; fix or remove the handoff records in {succ.default_state_dir()} by hand")
    return base | ack_adoption(lead)[0]


def label_queries(lead: str) -> list[str]:
    """The ids worth one `paseo ls --label ade.lead=<id>` call: the lead and its nearest predecessors (bounded), plus any
    adopted acknowledged predecessor."""
    try:
        ids = succ.recent_lineage(lead)
    except succ.SuccessionError as e:
        raise Refused(f"{e}; fix or remove the handoff records in {succ.default_state_dir()} by hand")
    adopted = ack_adoption(lead)[0]
    try:
        for pred in succ.acknowledged_predecessors(lead):  # bounded like the base path: each adopted predecessor's nearest ones
            if pred in adopted:
                ids += [x for x in succ.recent_lineage(pred) if x not in ids]
    except succ.SuccessionError as e:
        raise Refused(f"{e}; fix or remove the handoff records in {succ.default_state_dir()} by hand")
    return ids


def member_windows_by_lead(leads: list[str]) -> dict[str, set[str]]:
    """For each of `leads`: window ids that hold a live agent labelled ade.lead=<it> (from its state file); one `ls` each."""
    out: dict[str, set[str]] = {}
    for lead in leads:
        ids = [r["id"] for r in (paseo_json(["ls", "-g", "--json", "--label", f"ade.lead={lead}"]) or [])
               if isinstance(r, dict) and isinstance(r.get("id"), str) and r.get("status") != "closed"]
        out[lead] = {st["workspaceId"] for st in map(state_file, ids) if st and isinstance(st.get("workspaceId"), str)}
    return out


def _state_copy(path: Path) -> dict | None:
    """One Paseo state file as a dict, None when it cannot be read."""
    try:
        data = json.loads(path.read_text())
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None
    return data if isinstance(data, dict) else None


def _owner_of(rec: dict) -> str | None:
    labels = rec.get("labels")
    owner = labels.get("ade.lead") if isinstance(labels, dict) else None
    return owner if isinstance(owner, str) and owner else None


def foreign_agents(wks: str, lead: str) -> list[str]:
    """Agents in window `wks` (closed ones too: a closed worker still says whose window it was) labelled
    ade.lead=<another lead> (not this lead or one it replaced). An agent with several state files (Paseo writes a moved record's
    new file before it unlinks the old one) is judged copy by copy, live or closed alike: it counts when a copy naming `wks`
    carries another lead's label; copies that all name other windows put it elsewhere; a live agent with an unreadable copy has
    an unknown window and counts (fail closed; adversary PR 926 r2 LOW-1)."""
    mine = lineage(lead)
    out = []
    for a in live_agents():
        paths = state_paths(a["id"])
        if len(paths) > 1:
            copies = [_state_copy(p) for p in paths]
            owners = [_owner_of(c) for c in copies if c and c.get("workspaceId") == wks]
            other = next((o for o in owners if o and o not in mine), None)
            if other:
                out.append(f"{a['id']} (ade.lead={other}, two Paseo state files)")
            elif a.get("status") != "closed" and any(c is None for c in copies):
                out.append(f"{a['id']} ({a.get('status')}, two Paseo state files, one unreadable: its window is unknown, it may be in this one)")
            continue
        st = state_file(a["id"])
        if not st or st.get("workspaceId") != wks:
            continue
        owner = _owner_of(st)
        if owner and owner not in mine:
            out.append(f"{a['id']} (ade.lead={owner})")
    return out


def unclaimed_agents(wks: str, lead: str) -> list[str]:
    """Agents in window `wks` (any status) that are not labelled ade.lead=<lead or a lead it replaced>: the operator's or
    someone's hand launch."""
    mine = lineage(lead)
    out = []
    for a in live_agents():
        st = state_file(a["id"])
        if not st or not WKS_RE.fullmatch(str(st.get("workspaceId", ""))):
            if a.get("status") != "closed":
                out.append(f"{a['id']} ({a.get('status')}, no usable workspaceId: it may be in this window)")
            continue
        if st.get("workspaceId") != wks:
            continue
        labels = st.get("labels")
        if (labels.get("ade.lead") if isinstance(labels, dict) else None) not in mine:
            out.append(f"{a['id']} ({a.get('status')})")
    return out


def esc(text) -> str:
    """Text from Paseo for a refusal: control characters as escapes (a window name is `!r`; a path keeps its quotes off)."""
    return "".join(c if c.isprintable() else repr(c)[1:-1] for c in str(text))


def row_wks(row: dict) -> str:
    if not WKS_RE.fullmatch(str(row.get("workspaceId", ""))):
        raise Refused(f"window {row['name']!r} has no usable workspaceId")
    return row["workspaceId"]


def legacy_target(row: dict, legacy, repo: str | None, explicit: bool) -> str:
    """The current-form name for a legacy window: --repo when given, else the repo of the window's own cwd, else `repo`."""
    r = repo if explicit or not row.get("cwd") else wsn.repo_of(row["cwd"])
    if not r:
        raise Refused(f"legacy window {row['name']!r}: pass --repo (it has no cwd to take the repo from)")
    try:
        return wsn.migrated_name(legacy, r)
    except ValueError as e:
        raise Refused(f"legacy window {row['name']!r} cannot be renamed: {e}")


class Found(NamedTuple):
    row: dict
    rename_to: str | None  # the current-form name when the window still has a legacy one
    owned: bool            # positive evidence it is this lead's (legacy name with its id, registry, or its labelled live agent)


def find_window(lead: str, repo: str | None, middle: str | None, explicit: bool = False, cwd: str | None = None,
                box: str = "WORKER", pick: str | None = None, per_repo: bool = False) -> Found | None:
    """The lead's window of `box` (WORKER or OTHER; a LEAD window is the lead's own, `own_window`). Matches by exact name
    `<KIND> <repo> (<middle>)` (any repo when `repo` is None) or, without `middle`, by ownership; a legacy name carrying <lead>
    matches too; the 2026-11-13 kinds (WORKERS, USER) match as their box and come back with `rename_to` set. A launch passes
    `middle=None` (one box per lead and repo, whatever the slice or work) and `pick` (its --window-middle): `pick` chooses
    among several owned boxes by their `(<work>)` text and is never a reason to open another; `per_repo` (a launch) drops a
    box of another repo (by name, else by checkout), so a launch for a repo the lead has no box for opens that repo's box. Ownership is evidence, never a name: the lead's
    window record (written when the helper mints or migrates a window, and by a launch into an existing WORKERS window), a live agent labelled ade.lead=<lead> in it, or the
    lead id in a legacy name. Refused: two matches; a window registered to another lead or holding any agent (closed
    included) labelled for another lead; a `middle` that matches nothing while the lead owns another window (a typo must not
    open a second one, and only a window of the launch's own `repo` counts: one WORKERS window per (lead, repo), so a launch
    for a repo the lead has no window for mints one; windows only a predecessor placed do not count either, so a successor opens
    a new one for new work; a window whose repo cannot be read counts, and with `repo` None every owned window counts). With several
    owned windows and no `middle`, `repo` narrows them to that repo's (one match picks it). A name match with no evidence either way is returned with owned=False: a launch may adopt it, an
    archive never does."""
    mine = lineage(lead)
    labelled = member_windows_by_lead(label_queries(lead))
    members = set().union(*labelled.values()).union(*(read_registry(registry_path(x)) for x in mine))
    others = other_leads_windows(mine)
    own_ids = labelled.get(lead, set()) | read_registry(registry_path(lead))  # not inherited from a predecessor
    owned: list[dict] = []
    owned_own: list[dict] = []  # the subset the lead itself placed (or labelled): a typo must not open a second window
    own_cwd: dict[str, str | None] = {}  # window id -> its recorded cwd
    own_repo: dict[str, str | None] = {}  # window id -> its repo (the name's, else a legacy window's cwd's), None when unreadable
    hits: list[tuple[dict, str | None, Refused | None]] = []
    for row in list_windows():
        cur = wsn.parse(row["name"])
        legacy = None if cur else wsn.parse_legacy(row["name"])
        if cur and cur.box == box:
            by_member = row.get("workspaceId") in members
            by_name = middle is not None and cur.work == middle and (repo is None or cur.repo == repo)
            if by_member:
                owned.append(row)
                if row.get("workspaceId") in own_ids:
                    owned_own.append(row)
                    own_repo[row.get("workspaceId")] = cur.repo
                    own_cwd[row.get("workspaceId")] = row.get("cwd")
            if by_name or (middle is None and by_member):
                hits.append((row, None, None))
        elif legacy and wsn.BOX_OF[legacy.kind] == box and legacy.lead in mine:
            owned.append(row)
            if legacy.lead == lead:
                owned_own.append(row)
                own_cwd[row.get("workspaceId")] = row.get("cwd")
                own_repo[row.get("workspaceId")] = wsn.repo_of(row["cwd"]) if row.get("cwd") and os.path.isdir(row["cwd"]) else None  # a gone directory names no repo
            try:  # the new name is built for a hit only: an unbuildable legacy name must not block unrelated calls
                new, err = legacy_target(row, legacy, repo, explicit), None
            except Refused as e:
                new, err = None, e
            lm = legacy.middle.strip()
            names_it = err is not None and middle is not None and (lm == middle or any(
                wsn.normalize_work(lm, r) == middle for r in {repo, os.path.basename(row.get("cwd") or "")} if r))
            if middle is None or (new is not None and wsn.parse(new).work == middle) or names_it:  # unbuildable but for this work: refuse
                hits.append((row, new, err))
    # Windows only a predecessor placed are inherited, not windows this lead placed, so they do not trigger the typo guard: new
    # work gets a new window (2026-11-14, lead 8dcd57f4 stuck with four inherited windows). A window becomes the lead's own while
    # one of its live workers sits in it (labelled[lead]), or from the launch that places a worker in it (register_window below).
    # One WORKERS window per (lead, repo): a typo guards only against a second window for the SAME repo. A launch for a repo the
    # lead has no window for mints one (2026-11-14, tendcf lead 698fa914: a libntech worker was refused for a cfengine-core window
    # and had to run in it). A window whose repo cannot be read still counts, and `repo` None keeps every owned window counting.
    def by_name(r: dict) -> bool:  # names compare without case (`--repo CFEngine-core` is the repo `cfengine-core`)
        theirs = own_repo.get(r.get("workspaceId"))
        return theirs is None or theirs.casefold() == (repo or "").casefold()

    if middle is not None and not hits and owned_own:  # computed only when the guard can fire: it runs git for a window of another name
        mine_co = wsn.primary_checkout_of(cwd) if cwd else None
        if mine_co and os.path.realpath(wsn._git(mine_co, "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel") or "/nonexistent") != mine_co:
            mine_co = None  # not a git toplevel (a scratch directory, `~`): it names no repo, so nothing aliases to it

        def by_checkout(r: dict) -> bool:
            # the same git checkout under another name (a window named with a `--repo` alias): one window per repo, whatever it is called
            wc = own_cwd.get(r.get("workspaceId"))
            return bool(mine_co and wc and os.path.isdir(wc) and wsn.primary_checkout_of(wc) == mine_co)
        same_repo = [r for r in owned_own if repo is None or by_name(r) or by_checkout(r)]
        if same_repo:
            ids = ", ".join(f"{row_wks(r)} ({r['name']!r})" for r in same_repo)
            hint = "use that --window-middle (or none), not a second window"
            if repo is not None and not any(by_name(r) for r in same_repo):
                hint = (f"it is the same checkout as --cwd, so a window for {repo} needs --cwd that repo's own checkout; "
                        "otherwise use that --window-middle (or none), not a second window")
            raise Refused(f"no WORKERS window is named for work {middle!r}, but this lead has {ids}; {hint}")
    def hit_repo(h, live: bool = False):  # a repo known from evidence: the name, else (a legacy window) its cwd; never the argument itself
        cur = wsn.parse(h[0]["name"])
        if cur:
            return cur.repo
        if live and explicit:
            return repo  # a launch with --repo: legacy_target renames the legacy window to that repo, so it is that repo's
        if live and not (h[0].get("cwd") and os.path.isdir(h[0]["cwd"])):
            return None  # a launch: a legacy window whose directory is gone names no repo, so it still counts (it may be this one's)
        r = wsn.repo_of(h[0]["cwd"]) if h[0].get("cwd") else None
        return r if r and (not live or wsn.REPO_RE.fullmatch(r)) else None  # a directory that names no valid repo counts for any

    if per_repo and repo is not None and hits:  # one box per (lead, repo): a box of another repo is not this launch's
        co = wsn.primary_checkout_of(cwd) if cwd else None

        def same_repo_hit(h) -> bool:
            theirs = hit_repo(h, live=True)
            if theirs is None or theirs.casefold() == repo.casefold():  # an unreadable repo still counts (it may be this one)
                return True
            wc = h[0].get("cwd")  # the same git checkout under another name (a `--repo` alias); an explicit --repo names its own repo
            return bool(not explicit and co and wc and os.path.isdir(wc) and os.path.realpath(wsn._git(co, "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel") or "/nonexistent") == co
                        and wsn.primary_checkout_of(wc) == co)
        hits = [h for h in hits if same_repo_hit(h)]
    if len(hits) > 1 and pick is not None:  # several owned boxes: --window-middle (an old invocation) says which
        picked = [h for h in hits if (wsn.parse(h[1] or h[0]["name"]) or wsn.Name("", "", "")).work == pick]
        if picked:
            hits = picked
    if len(hits) > 1:  # a duplicate unclaimed name must not lock the lead out of its own window
        own_hits = [h for h in hits if h[1] is not None or h[0].get("workspaceId") in members]
        if len(own_hits) == 1:
            hits = own_hits
    if len(hits) > 1 and repo and middle is None:  # several owned windows, no work named: the one(s) of this repo
        for_repo = [h for h in hits if (hit_repo(h) or "").casefold() == repo.casefold()]
        if for_repo:  # one match picks it; several are still ambiguous, but only among this repo's windows
            hits = for_repo
    if len(hits) > 1:
        ids = ", ".join(f"{row_wks(r)} ({r['name']!r})" for r, _, _ in hits)
        raise Refused(f"{len(hits)} windows match the lead's {box} box: {ids}; pass --repo (or --window-middle, a work text "
                      "above) to pick one, or archive the extras (`ade-tidy --apply`, docs/workspace-layout.md)")
    if not hits:
        return None
    row, new, err = hits[0]
    if err is not None:
        raise err
    wks = row_wks(row)
    if wks in others:
        why = ack_adoption(lead)[1].get(others[wks])  # an acknowledged predecessor not adopted: say why (hf-38c)
        note = f"; its acknowledged handoff to {lead} is not followed because {why}" if why else ""
        raise Refused(f"window {wks} ({row['name']!r}) is registered to lead {others[wks]}, not {lead}{note} "
                      "(pick a different --window-middle)")
    owned_here = new is not None or wks in members
    if new is None:  # a current-form name: prove it is not another lead's
        foreign = foreign_agents(wks, lead)
        if foreign:
            raise Refused(f"window {wks} ({row['name']!r}) holds another lead's agents: {', '.join(foreign)}; "
                          "it is not this lead's WORKERS window (pick a different --window-middle)")
        if not owned_here:  # an unclaimed name: adoptable only when nothing foreign to this lead is in it
            strangers = unclaimed_agents(wks, lead)
            if strangers:
                raise Refused(f"window {wks} ({row['name']!r}) holds agents not labelled for this lead: {', '.join(strangers)}; "
                              "it may be the operator's or another lead's. Pick a different --window-middle, or archive "
                              "those agents first")
    cur_hit = wsn.parse(row["name"])
    if new is None and cur_hit and not cur_hit.current:  # `WORKERS r (w)` -> `WORKER r (w)`: renamed when a launch reuses it
        try:
            new = wsn.current_name(cur_hit)
        except ValueError as e:
            raise Refused(f"window {wks} ({row['name']!r}) cannot be renamed to its current kind: {e}; rename it by hand")
    return Found(row, new, owned_here)


def state_paths(agent_id: str) -> list[Path]:
    home = Path(os.environ.get("PASEO_HOME") or Path.home() / ".paseo")
    return sorted((home / "agents").glob(f"*/{agent_id}.json"))


def state_file(agent_id: str) -> dict | None:
    """The agent's Paseo state record, or None when there is none, it cannot be read, or the id has MORE THAN ONE file: Paseo
    writes a moved record's new file before it unlinks the old one and ignores an unlink error, so a stale copy can name another
    window, and picking one of the two would let `archive-window` skip a running worker (adversary PR 910 LOW-2). None is an
    unknown window: the archive check blocks on it, and so does `unclaimed_agents` for a live agent; `foreign_agents` reads each
    copy instead and refuses only a window a copy names (adversary PR 926 LOW-2, r2 LOW-1)."""
    files = state_paths(agent_id)
    if len(files) != 1:
        return None
    try:
        data = json.loads(files[0].read_text())
    except (OSError, ValueError):
        return None
    return data if isinstance(data, dict) else None


def state_dir() -> Path:
    d = Path(os.environ.get("ADE_WORKER_RUN_STATE") or Path.home() / ".local/state/ade/worker-run")
    d.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)
    return d


class Locks:
    """The lead's own lock, then one global lock: window ownership is read and written across leads, so a lead's find+launch
    and find+archive never interleave with another lead's (lock order is always lead, then global)."""

    def __init__(self, lead: str):
        d = state_dir()
        self.fhs = []
        for name in (f"{lead}.lock", "_global.lock"):
            fh = (d / name).open("a")
            self.fhs.append(fh)
            fcntl.flock(fh, fcntl.LOCK_EX)

    def close(self) -> None:
        for fh in reversed(self.fhs):
            fh.close()


def lock_for(lead: str) -> Locks:
    return Locks(lead)


def registry_path(lead: str) -> Path:
    return state_dir() / f"{lead}.windows.json"


def read_registry(path: Path) -> set[str]:
    try:
        data = json.loads(path.read_text())
        ids = data["windows"]
        if not isinstance(ids, list) or not all(isinstance(i, str) and WKS_RE.fullmatch(i) for i in ids):
            raise ValueError("bad window id")
        return set(ids)
    except FileNotFoundError:
        return set()
    except (OSError, ValueError, KeyError, TypeError):
        raise Refused(f"the window ownership record {path} is unreadable; ownership of windows is unknown, so nothing is "
                      "placed, renamed or archived (fix or remove that file by hand)")


def write_registry(lead: str, ids: set[str]) -> None:
    """Atomic: a temp file next to the record, then rename."""
    path = registry_path(lead)
    fd, tmp = tempfile.mkstemp(dir=path.parent, prefix=path.name + ".")
    try:
        with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as fh:
            json.dump({"windows": sorted(ids)}, fh)
        os.replace(tmp, path)
    except BaseException:
        Path(tmp).unlink(missing_ok=True)
        raise


def register_window(lead: str, wks: str) -> None:
    write_registry(lead, read_registry(registry_path(lead)) | {wks})


def other_leads_windows(mine: set[str]) -> dict[str, str]:
    """Window id -> the other lead that registered it (`mine`: the lead and the archived leads it replaced are not other)."""
    out: dict[str, str] = {}
    for path in state_dir().glob("*.windows.json"):
        owner = path.name[:-len(".windows.json")]
        if owner not in mine and LEAD_RE.fullmatch(owner):  # a stray file is not a lead's record
            for wks in read_registry(path):
                out.setdefault(wks, owner)
    return out


def check_caller(lead: str, on_behalf: bool) -> None:
    """--lead is the caller's own agent id; a different one (a stale id in a brief) needs --on-behalf-of-lead."""
    caller = os.environ.get("PASEO_AGENT_ID")
    if caller and caller != lead and not on_behalf:
        raise Refused(f"--lead {lead} is not this agent ({caller}); a wrong id would place or archive workers in another "
                      "lead's window and label them for it. Pass --on-behalf-of-lead if that is intended")


def passthrough_check(args: list[str]) -> None:
    if not args:
        raise Refused("nothing after `--`: pass the paseo run arguments (provider, mode, brief ...)")
    if args[0] in ("paseo", "run"):
        raise Refused("pass the paseo run arguments only, without a leading `paseo run` "
                      "(a plan's Choice.dispatch minus that prefix)")
    if not args[0].startswith("-"):
        raise Refused("the first argument after `--` must be a paseo run flag (flags before the brief; a Choice.dispatch "
                      "string is passed split into argv, not as one token)")
    if not any(a in DETACH_FLAGS for a in args):
        raise Refused("pass --no-wait: a foreground paseo run would hold this lead's launch lock until the worker ends")
    for i, a in enumerate(args):
        flag = a.split("=", 1)[0]
        if flag == "--prompt-file":
            raise Refused("paseo run has no --prompt-file: read the brief file and pass its text as one final positional argument")
        if re.fullmatch(r"-[A-Za-z][^\s]+", flag):  # a bundled short option (-oyaml, -qd) would hide an owned one
            raise Refused(f"{flag}: pass short options separately (-d, -m x), never bundled")
        if flag in OWNED_FLAGS:
            raise Refused(f"{flag} is set by ade-worker-run; do not pass it")
        if flag == "--label":
            value = a.split("=", 1)[1] if "=" in a else (args[i + 1] if i + 1 < len(args) else "")
            key = value.split("=", 1)[0]
            if key != key.strip() or any(c.isspace() for c in key):
                raise Refused(f"--label key {key!r} must not contain whitespace")
            if key in OWNED_LABEL_KEYS:
                raise Refused(f"--label {value.split('=', 1)[0]}=... is set by ade-worker-run; do not pass it")


def own_window(lead: str, why: str) -> dict:
    """The lead's own window (its tab row), from the lead's agent record, never from a possibly-unset PASEO_WORKSPACE_ID."""
    caller = os.environ.get("PASEO_AGENT_ID")
    if not caller or caller != lead:
        raise Refused(f"{why} resolves the window from the calling lead's own agent record: run it as the lead itself "
                      f"(PASEO_AGENT_ID must be --lead; got {caller or 'unset'}), without --on-behalf-of-lead")
    state = state_file(lead)
    wks = state.get("workspaceId") if state else None
    if not isinstance(wks, str) or not WKS_RE.fullmatch(wks):
        raise Refused(f"no usable workspaceId in the state file of agent {lead}, so its own window is unknown")
    row = next((r for r in list_windows() if r.get("workspaceId") == wks), None)
    if row is None:
        raise Refused(f"window {wks} (agent {lead}'s own) is not in `paseo workspace ls --json`")
    return row


_BARE_LEAD = re.compile(r"LEAD (\S(?:.*\S)?)")  # `LEAD tendcf`: the kind and a middle, no `<repo> (<work>)` shape (never a parsed name)


def main_target(row: dict, repo: str | None, explicit: bool, work: str | None, correct: bool = False) -> str | None:
    """The `LEAD <repo> (<work>)` name the lead's own window should have, or None when it already has it. A 2026-11-13
    `MAIN <repo> (<work>)` or `MAIN <middle>` name comes back as its LEAD name; so does a bare `LEAD <middle>`. The repo is
    --repo (`explicit`), else the window cwd's repo: never the home directory's name, and for a bare `LEAD <repo>` name over a cwd that
    is not a git repo, the name's own middle (`LEAD tendcf` in $HOME is repo `tendcf`). `correct` (rename-lead): an explicit --repo or
    `work` (--window-middle) that differs from a name already in the current form builds the corrected name instead of None.
    Refuses a WORKER or OTHER window (the lead's own tab row is never one of those)."""
    name = row["name"]
    cur = wsn.parse(name)
    if cur:
        if cur.box != "LEAD":
            raise Refused(f"the lead's own window {row['workspaceId']} is named {name!r} ({cur.kind}); a lead lives in a LEAD "
                          "window: rename it by hand if that is really the lead's window")
        new_repo, new_work = (repo if explicit and repo else cur.repo), (work if work is not None else cur.work)
        if cur.current and not (correct and (new_repo, new_work) != (cur.repo, cur.work)):
            return None
        try:
            return build_name("LEAD", new_repo, new_work) if correct else wsn.current_name(cur)
        except (ValueError, Refused) as e:
            raise Refused(f"the lead's own window {row['workspaceId']} ({name!r}) cannot be renamed to its current kind: {e}; rename it by hand")
    legacy = wsn.parse_legacy(name)
    if legacy and legacy.kind == "WORKERS":
        raise Refused(f"the lead's own window {row['workspaceId']} is named {name!r}, a workers window; rename it by hand")
    bare = _BARE_LEAD.fullmatch(name)
    middle = legacy.middle if legacy else (bare.group(1) if bare else None)
    cwd = row.get("cwd")
    if explicit or not cwd:
        r = repo
    else:
        home = same_dir(cwd, str(Path.home()))
        in_repo = not home and bool(wsn._git(cwd, "rev-parse", "--git-common-dir"))
        name_repo = bare.group(1) if bare and wsn.REPO_RE.fullmatch(bare.group(1)) else None
        if in_repo or (not home and not name_repo):
            r = wsn.repo_of(cwd)
        elif name_repo:
            r = name_repo  # not in a git repo: the name already says which repo this is
        else:
            raise Refused(f"pass --repo: the window's cwd {cwd} is the home directory, whose name is not a repo")
    if not r:
        raise Refused("pass --repo: the window has no cwd to take the repo name from")
    if work is None:
        work = wsn.normalize_work(middle if middle is not None else name, r)
        if bare and work == r:
            work = "lead"  # `LEAD tendcf` held no work text: the middle was the repo
    return build_name("LEAD", r, work)


def rename_main(opts) -> int:
    """Name the lead's own window `LEAD <repo> (<work>)` when it does not already have that name (MAIN -> LEAD included)."""
    check_names(opts.lead, None)
    lock = lock_for(opts.lead)
    try:
        row = own_window(opts.lead, "rename-main")
        new = main_target(row, opts.repo, bool(opts.repo), opts.window_middle, correct=True)
        if new is None:
            print(json.dumps({"renamed": False, "workspaceId": row["workspaceId"], "windowName": row["name"]}))
            return 0
        run_ok(["workspace", "rename", row["workspaceId"], new])
        print(json.dumps({"renamed": True, "workspaceId": row["workspaceId"], "windowName": new, "previousName": row["name"]}))
        return 0
    finally:
        lock.close()


def brief_index(rest: list[str]) -> int | None:
    """Index of the brief in the `paseo run` arguments, or None when the last argument cannot be told to be one: the brief is the last
    argument, after every flag (it follows a boolean flag, a `--flag=value`, or the value of a value flag)."""
    if not rest or rest[-1].startswith("-"):
        return None
    prev = rest[-2] if len(rest) > 1 else ""
    after_flag = (prev in BOOL_FLAGS and not (len(rest) > 2 and rest[-3] in VALUE_FLAGS)) or (prev.startswith("-") and "=" in prev) or \
        (not prev.startswith("-") and len(rest) > 2 and rest[-3] in VALUE_FLAGS)  # `--provider X BRIEF`
    return len(rest) - 1 if after_flag else None


def add_footer(rest: list[str]) -> list[str]:
    """Append the delivery-footer pointer to the brief, the last `paseo run` argument."""
    if not FOOTER.is_file():
        raise Refused(f"{FOOTER} does not exist; pass --no-footer to launch without the footer line")
    if brief_index(rest) is None:
        raise Refused("cannot tell which argument is the brief (the last one must be the brief, after every flag): "
                      "put it last, or pass --no-footer and carry the footer line yourself")
    last = rest[-1]
    if str(FOOTER) in last:
        return rest
    return [*rest[:-1], f"{last}\n\nAlso follow every item of {FOOTER}."]


REFUSED_REPORT_BASENAME = re.compile(r"^(REPORT|SUMMARY|FINDINGS|ANALYSIS)", re.IGNORECASE)  # Claude Code refuses a Write of these .md names
# The brief's OWN report path is read from labelled lines only (operator ruling 2026-11-22, PR 935 LOW-4): a path merely mentioned as an
# input (another agent's `~/.local/state/agent-reports/x/old-report.md`) is not the report. Labels: a line-start `Report:` / `Report path:`
# / `Report file:` (list marker or markdown around it allowed; the path may sit on the next line, after at most one blank line), a
# `## Report path` heading with the path on the next line (one blank line allowed), "write|save your report [file] to|at|in|as[:] <path>",
# and `{report} = <path>`. The path is absolute, `~/` or `$HOME/`. A line quoted with `>` is untrusted pasted content and labels nothing.
# Every labelled path is collected: two different ones are refused (PR 935 r3 LOW-2), never resolved by position.
_PATH = r"(?P<p>(?:/|~/|\$HOME/)[\w.@+~/-]+)"  # a label counts only when a PATH follows it: absolute, ~/ or $HOME/
_P = r"[ \t]*[`'\"]?" + _PATH
_LIST = r"^[ \t*#`_-]*(?:[A-Za-z]?\d+[a-z]?[.)][ \t]+)?"
_DELIVERABLE = r"(?:full\s+)?(?:report(?:\s+file)?|deliverable)"
BRIEF_REPORT_LABELS = [re.compile(x, re.IGNORECASE | re.MULTILINE) for x in (
    _LIST + r"report\b(?:[ \t]+(?:path|file)\b)?[*_`]*[ \t]*(?:is\b[ \t]*|[:=][*_`]*(?:[ \t]*\n(?:[ \t]*\n)?)?[ \t]*)[`'\"]?" + _PATH,
    r"^#+[ \t]*report[ \t]+(?:path|file)[ \t]*\n(?:[ \t]*\n)?" + _P,
    r"\b(?:write|save)\s+(?:your|the|a|its)\s+" + _DELIVERABLE + r"\s+(?:to|at|in|as)\s*:?\s*[`'\"]?" + _PATH,
    r"\{report\}\s*[=:]" + _P)]
BRIEF_DONE_LABELS = [re.compile(x, re.IGNORECASE | re.MULTILINE) for x in (  # no bare `Done:`: it is a status-line word
    _LIST + r"done[ \t]+(?:marker|file|path)\b[*_`]*[ \t]*[:=][*_`]*(?:[ \t]*\n(?:[ \t]*\n)?)?[ \t]*[`'\"]?" + _PATH,
    r"\{done\}\s*[=:]" + _P)]
SAFE_PATH = re.compile(r"[\w./@+~-]+")  # no space or quote: the worker copies the path into a Write call as given
VALUES_MARK = "Footer values:"


def _quoted(brief: str, pos: int) -> bool:
    """True when the line holding `pos` is a `>` blockquote line."""
    return brief[brief.rfind("\n", 0, pos) + 1:].lstrip(" \t").startswith(">")


def _labelled_paths(brief: str, labels: list, what: str) -> list[str]:
    """Every distinct path the brief labels (any of `labels`, outside `>` quotes), `~/` expanded, in order of first appearance.
    A path that is not a plain absolute one is refused, naming the label it came from."""
    found: list[tuple[int, str, str]] = []
    for rx in labels:
        for m in rx.finditer(brief):
            if not _quoted(brief, m.start()):
                found.append((m.start(), m.group("p").rstrip(".,"), " ".join(brief[m.start():m.start("p")].split())))
    paths: list[str] = []
    for _, raw, label in sorted(found):
        path = os.path.expanduser("~/" + raw[len("$HOME/"):] if raw.startswith("$HOME/") else raw)
        if not os.path.isabs(path) or ".." in path.split("/") or has_control_char(path) or not SAFE_PATH.fullmatch(path):
            raise Refused(f"the brief's labelled {what} path {raw!r} (label {label!r}) is not a plain absolute path (no `..`, spaces or quotes)")
        if path not in paths:
            paths.append(path)
    return paths


def _one_label(brief: str, labels: list, what: str) -> str | None:
    paths = _labelled_paths(brief, labels, what)
    if len(paths) > 1:
        raise Refused(f"the brief labels {len(paths)} {what} paths: {', '.join(paths)}; keep one (a quoted or pasted label can "
                      "override the real one, so the tool never picks by position)")
    return paths[0] if paths else None


def brief_footer_values(lead: str, brief: str) -> dict[str, str] | None:
    """The footer values for a brief that labels its own report path (see BRIEF_REPORT_LABELS), else None. {done} is the brief's
    labelled done marker (one that already exists is somebody's old file and is ignored), else `<report>.done`; {inbox} and {replies} sit
    beside the report. Nothing is generated or created."""
    report = _one_label(brief, BRIEF_REPORT_LABELS, "report")
    if report is None:
        return None
    dones = [d for d in _labelled_paths(brief, BRIEF_DONE_LABELS, "done marker") if not os.path.lexists(d)]
    if len(dones) > 1:
        raise Refused(f"the brief labels {len(dones)} done marker paths: {', '.join(dones)}; keep one")
    done = dones[0] if dones else report + ".done"
    return {"lead": lead, "report": report, "done": done, "inbox": report + ".inbox.md", "replies": report + ".replies.md"}


_MENTIONED_REPORT = re.compile(_PATH)


def mentioned_report_paths(brief: str) -> list[str]:
    """Absolute, `~/` or `$HOME/` paths in the brief that look like a report (`...-report.md` or under `agent-reports/`), for the
    warning printed when no label matched and a generated path is used instead."""
    out: list[str] = []
    for m in _MENTIONED_REPORT.finditer(brief):
        p = m.group("p").rstrip(".,")
        if (p.endswith("-report.md") or "/agent-reports/" in p) and p not in out:
            out.append(p)
    return out


def footer_report_paths(lead: str, slice_name: str) -> dict[str, str]:
    """The values the footer's placeholders take for this launch, by the layout agent_footer_gate uses:
    <report dir>/<lead id>/<slice>-report.md, .done / .inbox.md / .replies.md beside it. The report dir is
    $AGENT_FOOTER_REPORT_DIR (the gate's own override) else ~/.local/state/agent-reports. A slice whose report name Claude Code would
    refuse to Write (starts with report/summary/findings/analysis) gets a `worker-` prefix. Refused on a path with a control character."""
    base = Path(os.environ.get("AGENT_FOOTER_REPORT_DIR") or Path.home() / ".local/state/agent-reports")
    stem = f"worker-{slice_name}" if REFUSED_REPORT_BASENAME.match(slice_name) else slice_name
    if not SLICE_RE.fullmatch(slice_name):
        raise Refused(f"the slice name {slice_name!r} cannot name a report file")
    # A report or .done that already exists is someone's earlier (maybe finished) report (agent_footer_gate, 2026-10-18): never reused,
    # so a lead waiting on this launch's .done cannot be woken by a stale one. The next free `<stem>-N-report.md` is taken instead.
    for n in range(1, 1000):
        report = base / lead / (f"{stem}-report.md" if n == 1 else f"{stem}-{n}-report.md")
        if not report.exists() and not Path(str(report) + ".done").exists():
            break
    else:
        raise Refused(f"no free report name for slice {slice_name!r} under {base / lead}; clear the old reports")
    r = str(report)
    if has_control_char(r) or not SAFE_PATH.fullmatch(r):
        raise Refused(f"the report path {r!r} holds a space, quote or control character; "
                      "set AGENT_FOOTER_REPORT_DIR to a plain directory or pass --no-footer")
    return {"lead": lead, "report": r, "done": r + ".done", "inbox": r + ".inbox.md", "replies": r + ".replies.md"}


STUB_TEXT = "STATUS: working\n"


def reserve_report(values: dict[str, str]) -> tuple[int, int]:
    """Just before `paseo run`: make the report directory (a symlink, a non-directory or another user's directory is refused; a looser
    mode is tightened to 700) and create the report itself exclusively with `STATUS: working`, so two launches can never share a path and
    an existing report is never overwritten. An OS error is a refusal, not a traceback. Returns the stub's (device, inode)."""
    report = Path(values["report"])
    d = report.parent
    try:
        d.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True, mode=0o700)
        st = d.lstat()
        if stat.S_ISLNK(st.st_mode) or not stat.S_ISDIR(st.st_mode) or st.st_uid != os.getuid():
            raise Refused(f"{d} is not a directory of yours (a symlink or another user's); pass --no-footer or fix it")
        if st.st_mode & 0o077:
            d.chmod(0o700)
        fd = os.open(report, os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL, 0o600)
    except FileExistsError:
        raise Refused(f"{report} appeared while the launch was prepared; launch again")
    except OSError as e:
        raise Refused(f"cannot prepare the report {report}: {e}")
    with os.fdopen(fd, "w") as f:
        f.write(STUB_TEXT)
        st = os.fstat(f.fileno())
    return st.st_dev, st.st_ino


def add_footer_values(rest: list[str], values: dict[str, str], created: bool = False) -> list[str]:
    """Append the `Footer values:` line after the footer pointer, so the worker never meets an unfilled {report} / {done} / {lead}.
    `created`: ade-worker-run reserves the report file (`STATUS: working`), so the line says to Read it before overwriting it (Claude
    Code refuses a Write to an existing file the worker has not read)."""
    line = (f"{VALUES_MARK} " + "; ".join(f"{{{k}}} = {v}" for k, v in values.items())
            + ". Use these wherever the footer says {report}, {done}, {lead}, {inbox} or {replies}."
            + (" The {report} file already exists with `STATUS: working`: Read it, then overwrite it (footer item 1)." if created else ""))
    return [*rest[:-1], f"{rest[-1]}\n\n{line}"]


def has_control_char(p: str) -> bool:
    """True when the path holds a control, format or line/paragraph-separator character (a newline, U+2028 or U+2029 would split the
    brief line that names it; U+202E reverses how the rest of the path reads)."""
    return any(unicodedata.category(c) in ("Cc", "Cf", "Zl", "Zp") for c in p)


def add_cwd_line(rest: list[str], eff_cwd: str, cwd: str, explicit: bool) -> list[str]:
    """Tell the worker, in its brief, that its session starts in `eff_cwd` (the window's primary checkout, where nothing may be edited).
    `explicit` (the caller passed --cwd): the work belongs in `cwd`, and the line says to run every command there. Not explicit: `cwd`
    is only where the lead stands, usually its own claimed worktree, so the line names no work directory (the brief names the worker's).
    The line goes before the footer pointer ade-worker-run added (after the brief's own footer text when the brief already names
    docs/dispatch-footer.md: then no pointer is added). Paths are shell-quoted so a `cd` of them is safe to paste. When the last argument
    is not the brief (a flag value under --no-footer) the arguments are left alone and a warning says so."""
    if brief_index(rest) is None:
        sys.stderr.write("ade-worker-run: warning: cannot tell which argument is the brief, so it carries no note on where the session starts\n")
        return rest
    if explicit:
        line = (f"Your session starts in {shlex.quote(eff_cwd)}; run every command from {shlex.quote(cwd)} (cd there or git -C); "
                f"never edit or commit in {shlex.quote(eff_cwd)}.")
    else:
        line = (f"Your session starts in {shlex.quote(eff_cwd)}, the shared primary checkout: never edit or commit there; "
                "work only in the worktree your brief names.")
    last, tail = rest[-1], f"\n\nAlso follow every item of {FOOTER}."
    at = last.rfind(tail)
    if at >= 0 and (last[at + len(tail):] == "" or last[at + len(tail):].startswith(f"\n\n{VALUES_MARK} ")):
        return [*rest[:-1], f"{last[:at]}\n\n{line}{last[at:]}"]  # before the pointer and the values block ade-worker-run added
    return [*rest[:-1], f"{last}\n\n{line}"]


def same_dir(a: str, b: str) -> bool:
    """True when `a` and `b` name the same directory: the one comparator, `ade_claims.same_path` (samefile, so a symlink, a trailing
    slash and, on macOS's case-insensitive volume, a case-differing spelling all match; a missing path falls back to the textual
    realpath compare; an unusable path never matches, so a launch fails closed)."""
    return ade_claims.same_path(a, b)


def check_path_text(label: str, p: object) -> str:
    """Refuse, before anything is launched, a path that cannot be a file name (an embedded NUL, a lone surrogate)."""
    if not isinstance(p, str):
        raise Refused(f"{label} is not a path string")
    try:
        p.encode()
        os.fsencode(p)
    except (UnicodeEncodeError, ValueError):
        raise Refused(f"{label} is not a usable path (embedded NUL or an unencodable character): {p!r}")
    if "\0" in p:
        raise Refused(f"{label} is not a usable path (embedded NUL): {p!r}")
    return p


def names_path(brief: str, paths: list[str]) -> bool:
    """True when the brief carries one of `paths` as a whole absolute path (not a prefix of a longer name); every path passed is already absolute."""
    return any(re.search(r"(?<![\w/.-])" + re.escape(p.rstrip("/")) + r"(?![\w-]|\.[\w-])", brief) for p in paths if p)


def preflight_mode(args: list[str]) -> list[str]:
    """Validate explicit modes before any workspace mutation; labels are not IDs."""
    options = []
    i = 0
    while i < len(args):
        token = args[i]
        if token == "--" or not token.startswith("-"):
            break  # prompt text is never an option
        flag, sep, value = token.partition("=")
        end = i + 1
        if flag in VALUE_FLAGS and not sep:
            if end >= len(args):
                raise Refused(f"{flag} needs a value")
            value = args[end]
            end += 1
        options.append((flag, value, i, end))
        i = end
    modes = [o for o in options if o[0] == "--mode"]
    if not modes:
        return args
    providers = [o[1] for o in options if o[0] == "--provider"]
    if len(providers) != 1 or len(modes) != 1:
        raise Refused("explicit --mode requires exactly one --provider and one --mode")
    provider = providers[0].split("/", 1)[0]
    rows = paseo_json(["provider", "ls", "--json"])
    matches = [r for r in rows if isinstance(r, dict) and r.get("provider") == provider] if isinstance(rows, list) else []
    if len(matches) != 1:
        raise Refused(f"provider catalog missing or ambiguous for {provider!r}")
    row = matches[0]
    if row.get("enabled") not in (True, "Enabled") or row.get("status") not in ("ready", "available") or row.get("error"):
        raise Refused(f"provider {provider!r} catalog is not ready and enabled")
    catalog = row.get("modes")
    _, requested, start, end = modes[0]
    if catalog == [] or catalog == "":
        sys.stderr.write(f"ade-worker-run: provider {provider!r} has no modes; dropping --mode {requested!r}\n")
        return args[:start] + args[end:]
    if isinstance(catalog, str) and catalog.strip():
        # Current CLI flattens IDs to display labels. Do not invent IDs or break
        # existing valid launches: Paseo remains authoritative for nonempty modes.
        sys.stderr.write(f"ade-worker-run: provider {provider!r} catalog exposes mode labels only; "
                         "Paseo will validate the requested mode ID\n")
        return args
    if not isinstance(catalog, list) or any(not isinstance(m, dict) or not isinstance(m.get("id"), str) for m in catalog):
        raise Refused(f"provider {provider!r} mode catalog is malformed")
    if requested not in [m["id"] for m in catalog]:
        raise Refused(f"invalid --mode {requested!r} for provider {provider!r}")
    return args


def cleanup_failed_workspace(err: str, before: set[str]) -> None:
    """Archive only a uniquely identified, freshly minted, demonstrably empty box."""
    minted = set(CREATED_RE.findall(err))
    if len(minted) != 1:
        sys.stderr.write("ade-worker-run: failed-create cleanup: no unique created workspace; inspect manually\n")
        return
    wks = minted.pop()
    try:
        if wks in before:
            raise Refused("workspace existed before launch")
        rows = paseo_json(["ls", "-g", "--json"])
        if not isinstance(rows, list):
            raise Refused("live agent inventory unavailable")
        for row in rows:
            if not isinstance(row, dict) or not isinstance(row.get("id"), str):
                raise Refused("live agent inventory malformed")
            state = state_file(row["id"])
            workspace = row.get("workspaceId") or (state or {}).get("workspaceId")
            if not isinstance(workspace, str) or not WKS_RE.fullmatch(workspace) or workspace == wks:
                raise Refused("workspace is occupied or a live agent cannot be placed")
        run_ok(["workspace", "archive", wks])
        sys.stderr.write(f"ade-worker-run: archived failed-create workspace {wks}\n")
    except (Refused, OSError) as exc:
        sys.stderr.write(f"ade-worker-run: cleanup of {wks} failed: {exc}; inspect manually\n")


def launch(opts, rest: list[str]) -> int:
    lead, name = opts.lead, opts.slice
    check_names(lead, name)
    check_caller(lead, opts.on_behalf_of_lead)
    passthrough_check(rest)
    try:
        rest = mcpod.apply(rest, list(opts.mcp or []), lambda: paseo_json(["provider", "ls", "--json"]))
    except mcpod.McpError as e:
        raise Refused(str(e))
    bi = brief_index(rest)  # before the footer line: the footer names paths of its own
    brief = rest[bi] if bi is not None else ""  # no identifiable brief names no worktree (a moved launch is then refused)
    report_info: dict[str, str] | None = None
    report_generated = False
    reserved: tuple[int, int] | None = None  # (device, inode) of the stub reserve_report created, else None

    def drop_stub() -> None:
        """Remove the stub this launch created, only when it is still that file and still exactly `STATUS: working`: a brief's own
        labelled report (never created here) and a stub the worker already wrote to are left alone."""
        if reserved is None or not report_info:
            return
        stub = Path(report_info["report"])
        try:
            st = stub.lstat()
            if (st.st_dev, st.st_ino) == reserved and stub.read_text() == STUB_TEXT:
                stub.unlink()
        except OSError:
            pass
    if not opts.no_footer:
        rest = add_footer(rest)
        report_info = brief_footer_values(lead, brief)  # a labelled report path in the brief is the report: nothing is generated
        if report_info is None:
            report_info, report_generated = footer_report_paths(lead, name), True
            mentioned = mentioned_report_paths(brief)
            if mentioned:  # a label form this tool does not know would leave the worker two conflicting report paths
                sys.stderr.write(f"ade-worker-run: warning: no labelled report path in the brief, so {{report}} is the generated "
                                 f"{report_info['report']}, but the brief names {', '.join(mentioned[:3])}; if that is the report, "
                                 "label it (`Report: <path>`) and launch again\n")
        rest = add_footer_values(rest, report_info, created=report_generated)
    rest = preflight_mode(rest)
    main_place = opts.placement == "lead"
    box = "OTHER" if opts.placement == "other" else "WORKER"  # the box the window is looked up or opened in (not the lead's own)
    if main_place and opts.window_middle is not None:
        raise Refused("--window-middle names a box's (<work>) text; --placement lead launches into the lead's own window")
    cwd = os.path.realpath(check_path_text("--cwd", opts.cwd or os.getcwd()))
    repo = opts.repo or wsn.repo_of(cwd)
    work = opts.window_middle or DEFAULT_WORK[box]  # the (<work>) text of a box this launch opens; never a reason to open one
    if not main_place:
        build_name(box, repo, work)  # refuse a bad repo/work/over-long name before anything is launched
    worktree = opts.worktree or (cwd if opts.cwd and wsn.linked_worktree(cwd) else None)  # named in the tab, never used as a path
    lock = lock_for(lead)  # held to the end: launches and archive-window of one lead serialize (paseo run --no-wait is quick)
    try:
        rename_to, adopt = None, False
        if main_place:
            win = own_window(lead, "--placement main")
            rename_to = main_target(win, repo, bool(opts.repo), None)  # None: already `MAIN <repo> (<work>)`
            legacy = wsn.parse_legacy(win["name"])
            cur = wsn.parse(win["name"])
            if rename_to is not None and not ((legacy and legacy.kind == "MAIN") or (cur and not cur.current)):  # only a 2026-11-13 MAIN name is migrated
                raise Refused(f"the lead's own window {win['workspaceId']} is named {win['name']!r}, not `LEAD <repo> (<work>)`; "
                              f"run `ade-worker-run rename-main --lead {lead}` first (a worker started on the operator's "
                              "request goes in the LEAD window; only a 2026-11-13 `MAIN` name is renamed implicitly)")
        else:
            # One box per lead and repo, whatever the slice: --window-middle only names a box this launch opens, or picks among several
            # boxes the lead already owns (find_window `pick`); it never opens a second one (operator ruling 2026-11-14).
            found = find_window(lead, repo, None, bool(opts.repo), cwd, box=box, pick=opts.window_middle, per_repo=True)
            win, rename_to = (found.row, found.rename_to) if found else (None, None)
            adopt = bool(found and not found.owned)  # an unclaimed, empty window of this exact name: recorded once the launch succeeds
        if win is not None and win.get("cwd"):
            check_path_text(f"window {row_wks(win)}'s cwd", win["cwd"])  # before the launch: a bad path is a refusal, never a traceback after it
        redirected = False  # the window's own cwd is the repo's primary checkout of --cwd: placed there, the brief names the worktree
        if win is not None and not main_place and opts.cwd and win.get("cwd") and not same_dir(win["cwd"], cwd) \
                and same_dir(wsn.primary_checkout_of(cwd), win["cwd"]):
            redirected = True
        elif win is not None and opts.cwd and win.get("cwd") and not same_dir(win["cwd"], cwd):
            # `paseo run --workspace` takes the agent's cwd from the workspace and ignores --cwd (getpaseo/paseo#9699): a worker
            # started here would silently run in the window's directory, not the claimed worktree the caller named.
            raise Refused(f"window {row_wks(win)} ({win['name']!r}) runs in {esc(win['cwd'])}, but --cwd is {esc(cwd)}: paseo ignores --cwd "
                          f"when it places an agent in an existing window, so the worker would start in {esc(win['cwd'])}. Pass "
                          f"--cwd {esc(win['cwd'])} (or none) and give the worktree {esc(cwd)} as an absolute path in the brief "
                          "(docs/workspace-layout.md item 5: a window's cwd is its primary checkout, the writer works in the "
                          "claimed worktree by absolute paths)")
        # A minted window's cwd is its repo's primary checkout, never the claimed worktree the caller named (docs/workspace-layout.md
        # item 5): every later worker of the window defaults to that directory, so a worktree there would hand another writer a
        # claimed worktree (2026-11-14, wr-01). The worktree travels in the brief by absolute path, as for an existing window.
        if win is None:
            eff_cwd = wsn.primary_checkout_of(cwd)
        else:
            eff_cwd = os.path.realpath(win["cwd"]) if redirected else (cwd if opts.cwd else win.get("cwd") or cwd)
        check_path_text("the worker's directory", eff_cwd)
        moved = not same_dir(eff_cwd, cwd)  # one comparator: a case-variant spelling of --cwd is not a move (macOS APFS)
        # The caller asked for a directory (--cwd) or is standing in a linked worktree (no --cwd): the worker still starts in
        # eff_cwd, so the same checks and reports apply to both (2026-11-14, lead review of #709: the implicit case was silent).
        requested = bool(opts.cwd) or (win is None and not main_place and moved and wsn.linked_worktree(cwd))
        if moved and requested and (has_control_char(eff_cwd) or has_control_char(cwd)):  # both go into the worker's brief
            raise Refused(f"a directory name holds a control character (a newline would split the brief line that names it): "
                          f"{eff_cwd!r}, {cwd!r}")
        if moved and requested and not main_place:
            top = wsn._git(cwd, "rev-parse", "--show-toplevel")  # --cwd may be a subdirectory of the worktree the brief names
            if not names_path(brief, [cwd, os.path.abspath(os.path.expanduser(opts.cwd or cwd)), os.path.realpath(top) if top else ""]):
                # the worker starts in eff_cwd, the shared primary checkout where nothing may be edited: its brief must name the worktree
                if opts.cwd:
                    raise Refused(f"the worker would start in {eff_cwd} (the repo's primary checkout), not --cwd {cwd}, and the brief "
                                  f"does not name {cwd}: put that worktree in the brief as an absolute path so every repository "
                                  "operation runs there (docs/workspace-layout.md item 5), then launch again")
                # no --cwd: `cwd` is only where the lead stands, usually its own claimed worktree: never advise handing it over
                raise Refused(f"you gave no --cwd and stand in linked worktree {cwd}: the worker would start in {eff_cwd} (the repo's "
                              "primary checkout), and the brief does not name this worktree. Pass --cwd <the worker's own worktree> "
                              "and name it in the brief by absolute path, or run from the primary checkout "
                              "(docs/workspace-layout.md item 5). Never hand a worker the worktree you are working in")
        if rename_to:  # retroactive migration of a legacy name; the window id does not change
            if any(r["name"] == rename_to for r in list_windows() if r.get("workspaceId") != win.get("workspaceId")):
                raise Refused(f"cannot rename legacy window {win['name']!r} to {rename_to!r}: another window already has that "
                              "name (it would erase the only record of whose window this is); rename one by hand")
            if not main_place:
                register_window(lead, row_wks(win))  # ownership is recorded before the lead id leaves the name
            run_ok(["workspace", "rename", row_wks(win), rename_to])
            win = {**win, "name": rename_to}
        if win is None:
            wname = build_name(box, repo, work)
        else:
            wname = win["name"]
        tab = wsn.tab_name("OTHER" if box == "OTHER" and not main_place else "WORKER", name, lead, worktree)
        if moved and requested:
            sys.stderr.write(f"ade-worker-run: the worker starts in {eff_cwd} (the window's primary checkout), not {cwd}; "
                             "the brief carries the worktree\n")
        if moved and requested:  # the worker itself is told too: the stderr note above reaches only the launcher
            # the explicit form tells the worker to run every command from `cwd`: only right when that is a linked worktree, never a
            # --cwd inside the shared primary checkout (it would send the worker into the checkout the same line forbids editing)
            rest = add_cwd_line(rest, eff_cwd, cwd, bool(opts.cwd) and wsn.linked_worktree(cwd))
        place = ["--workspace", row_wks(win), "--cwd", eff_cwd] if win else ["--new-workspace", "local", "--cwd", eff_cwd]
        linked = win is None and not moved and wsn.linked_worktree(eff_cwd)
        if linked:
            sys.stderr.write(f"ade-worker-run: warning: no primary checkout found for {cwd}; the new window's cwd {eff_cwd} is a "
                             "linked worktree (a later worker of the window would start in it)\n")
        args = ["run", *place, "--label", f"ade.lead={lead}", "--label", f"slice={name}"]
        if main_place:
            args += ["--label", "ade.placement=main"]  # the label value keeps its 2026-11-13 spelling: tidy and the autoname hook read both
        elif box == "OTHER":
            args += ["--label", "ade.placement=other"]
        if "--json" not in rest:
            args.append("--json")
        before = {row_wks(r) for r in list_windows()} if win is None else set()
        if report_info:  # as late as possible: a launch refused above leaves nothing behind
            if report_generated:
                reserved = reserve_report(report_info)
            sys.stderr.write(f"ade-worker-run: report {report_info['report']} (done marker {report_info['done']})\n")
        rc, out, err = paseo([*args, *rest], timeout=300)
        if err:
            sys.stderr.write(err)
        if rc != 0:
            if win is None and "AGENT_CREATE_FAILED" in out + err:
                cleanup_failed_workspace(err, before)
            drop_stub()  # rc != 0: no agent was created, so no worker holds this path
            raise Refused(f"paseo run failed (rc {rc}): {out.strip()[:300]}")
        try:
            result = json.loads(out)
            agent_id = result["agentId"]
        except (ValueError, KeyError, TypeError):  # rc 0: an agent may exist and hold the stub's path, so the stub stays
            raise Refused("paseo run printed no agentId; check `paseo ls -g --json` for the new agent")
        if not isinstance(agent_id, str) or not LEAD_RE.fullmatch(agent_id):
            raise Refused("paseo run printed an unusable agentId (expected a UUID)")
        try:
            wks = resolve_window_id(win, result, err, agent_id)
            if win is not None and not main_place:  # a launch into an existing window (inherited, legacy, adopted) makes it this lead's own
                register_window(lead, wks)
            if win is None:
                register_window(lead, wks)  # the window is this lead's from the moment it exists
                run_ok(["workspace", "rename", wks, wname])
            run_ok(["agent", "update", agent_id, "--name", tab])
            if requested:  # paseo drops --cwd in an existing window and from inside an agent (getpaseo/paseo#9699): check where it landed
                got = agent_cwd(agent_id)
                want = eff_cwd if (win is None or redirected) else cwd
                if got and not same_dir(got, want):
                    stopped = stop_agent(agent_id)  # a fresh worker has done no work yet; running its brief in the wrong checkout is the harm
                    again = ("relaunch with the window's own --cwd" if win is not None else
                             "relaunch from the repo's primary checkout (paseo dropped --cwd for the new window)")
                    raise Refused(f"the worker started in {esc(got)}, not {esc(want)} (paseo ignored --cwd); it was "
                                  f"{'stopped (interrupted, not archived)' if stopped else 'NOT stopped: stop or archive it now'}; {again}")
        except (Refused, OSError) as e:
            raise Refused(f"{e} (agent {agent_id} was launched; fix its placement by hand)")
    finally:
        if lock is not None:
            lock.close()
    out = {"agentId": agent_id, "workspaceId": wks, "windowName": wname, "tabName": tab}
    if report_info:
        out.update({"reportPath": report_info["report"], "donePath": report_info["done"]})
    if moved and requested:  # the caller asked for another directory (or stood in one): say where the worker started
        out.update({"cwd": eff_cwd, "requestedCwd": cwd})
    print(json.dumps(out))
    return 0


def resolve_window_id(win: dict | None, result: dict, err: str, agent_id: str) -> str:
    """The window the launch landed in: structured when paseo prints it, else the one `Created workspace` line."""
    found = set()
    structured = result.get("workspaceId") if isinstance(result, dict) else None
    if structured is not None:
        if not isinstance(structured, str) or not WKS_RE.fullmatch(structured):
            raise Refused("paseo run printed an unusable workspaceId")
        found.add(structured)
    if win is not None:
        found.add(win["workspaceId"])
    else:
        found.update(CREATED_RE.findall(err))
        if not found:
            raise Refused("paseo run reported no created workspace (no JSON workspaceId, no `Created workspace wks_... -` line)")
    state = state_file(agent_id)
    if state and isinstance(state.get("workspaceId"), str):
        found.add(state["workspaceId"])
    if len(found) != 1:
        raise Refused(f"the launch's window id is ambiguous: {sorted(found)}")
    return found.pop()


def stop_agent(agent_id: str) -> bool:
    """Interrupt a worker that started in the wrong directory (`paseo agent stop`, a no-op when it is idle). True when it succeeded."""
    try:
        rc, _, _ = paseo(["agent", "stop", agent_id])
    except Refused:
        return False
    return rc == 0


def agent_cwd(agent_id: str) -> str | None:
    """The `Cwd` of a launched agent, None when paseo cannot say (never blocks a launch that already happened)."""
    try:
        rc, out, _ = paseo(["agent", "inspect", agent_id, "--json"])
        got = json.loads(out).get("Cwd") if rc == 0 else None
    except (Refused, ValueError, AttributeError):  # a timeout or unreadable answer: the launch stands
        return None
    return got if isinstance(got, str) and got else None


def run_ok(args: list[str]) -> None:
    rc, out, err = paseo(args)
    if rc != 0:
        raise Refused(f"paseo {' '.join(args[:2])} failed (rc {rc}): {err.strip() or out.strip()}")


def live_agents() -> list[dict]:
    rows = paseo_json(["ls", "-g", "--json"])  # no -a: archived agents are not listed
    if not isinstance(rows, list):
        raise Refused("paseo ls -g --json did not return a list")
    return [r for r in rows if isinstance(r, dict) and isinstance(r.get("id"), str)]


def archive_blockers(lead: str, wks: str, idle_handled: bool) -> list[str]:
    labelled = {}  # agent id -> the ade.lead=<id> label that matched (the lead or a nearby replaced predecessor)
    for x in label_queries(lead):
        for r in (paseo_json(["ls", "-g", "--json", "--label", f"ade.lead={x}"]) or []):
            if isinstance(r, dict) and isinstance(r.get("id"), str):
                labelled.setdefault(r["id"], x)
    blockers = []
    for a in live_agents():
        aid, status = a["id"], a.get("status")
        state = state_file(aid)
        in_window = bool(state) and state.get("workspaceId") == wks
        if status == "closed":
            # a closed agent of this lead's lineage never blocks, but one nobody here launched (the operator's session in the
            # OTHER box, a daemon-restart casualty) is archived with the window: it blocks like a live one
            if aid not in labelled:
                if in_window:
                    blockers.append(f"{aid}: closed, but not labelled for this lead (the archive would archive it with the window)")
                elif state is None or not WKS_RE.fullmatch(str(state.get("workspaceId", ""))):
                    # no readable state file or workspaceId: its window is unknown, so it may be in this one (fail closed, am-02)
                    blockers.append(f"{aid}: closed, not labelled for this lead, and no readable state file with a workspaceId, "
                                    "so its window is unknown (archive it with `paseo agent archive`, or restore its state file)")
            continue
        if state is None or not WKS_RE.fullmatch(str(state.get("workspaceId", ""))):
            blockers.append(f"{aid}: live ({status}) with no usable workspaceId in a state file, so its window is unknown")
            continue
        if not in_window:
            continue  # only the window's own agents block it: the archive touches nothing else, whatever lead or placement they carry
        if aid in labelled:
            if status == "idle" and idle_handled:
                continue
            blockers.append(f"{aid}: labelled ade.lead={labelled[aid]}, status {status}" +
                            (" (pass --idle-handled once its report is handled)" if status == "idle" else ""))
        elif in_window:
            blockers.append(f"{aid}: other live agent in the window, status {status}")
    return blockers


def archive_window(opts) -> int:
    check_names(opts.lead, None)
    check_caller(opts.lead, opts.on_behalf_of_lead)
    lock = lock_for(opts.lead)  # a launch of this lead cannot slip in between the check and the archive
    try:
        return archive_locked(opts)
    finally:
        lock.close()


def archive_locked(opts) -> int:
    box = "OTHER" if opts.placement == "other" else "WORKER"
    found = find_window(opts.lead, opts.repo, opts.window_middle, bool(opts.repo), box=box)
    if found is None:
        raise Refused(f"no {box} box for lead {opts.lead}" +
                      ("" if opts.window_middle else " (no window record or labelled agent finds it: pass --window-middle)"))
    win = found.row
    name = win["name"]
    cur = wsn.parse(name)
    legacy = wsn.parse_legacy(name)
    if not found.owned:
        raise Refused(f"window {win['workspaceId']} ({name!r}) has the right name but nothing shows it is lead {opts.lead}'s "
                      "(no window record, no live agent labelled for this lead): a name alone never confers ownership, "
                      "so it is not archived")
    if not ((cur and cur.box == box) or (legacy and wsn.BOX_OF[legacy.kind] == box and legacy.lead in lineage(opts.lead))):
        raise Refused(f"window {win['workspaceId']} is not a {box} box ({name!r}); a LEAD window is never archived here")
    mine = sorted(lineage(opts.lead))  # computed before the archive: a ledger gone cyclic meanwhile must not strand the record
    blockers = archive_blockers(opts.lead, win["workspaceId"], opts.idle_handled)
    if blockers:
        for b in blockers:
            sys.stderr.write(f"blocker: {b}\n")
        print(json.dumps({"archived": False, "workspaceId": win["workspaceId"], "windowName": name,
                          "blockers": blockers}))
        return 1
    if not opts.dry_run:
        run_ok(["workspace", "archive", win["workspaceId"]])
        for x in mine:  # the window may be recorded under a replaced lead (the global lock is held)
            recorded = read_registry(registry_path(x))
            if win["workspaceId"] in recorded:
                write_registry(x, recorded - {win["workspaceId"]})
    print(json.dumps({"archived": not opts.dry_run, "workspaceId": win["workspaceId"], "windowName": name,
                      "blockers": []}))
    return 0


def placement_arg(v: str) -> str:
    """The 2026-11-13 spellings (`workers`, `main`) still work."""
    return {"workers": "worker", "main": "lead"}.get(v, v)


def main(argv: list[str]) -> int:
    rest: list[str] = []
    if "--" in argv:
        i = argv.index("--")
        argv, rest = argv[:i], argv[i + 1:]
    if argv[:1] in (["rename-main"], ["rename-lead"]):
        p = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="ade-worker-run rename-main")
        p.add_argument("--lead", required=True)
        p.add_argument("--window-middle")
        p.add_argument("--repo")
        opts = p.parse_args(argv[1:])
        if rest:
            p.error("rename-main takes no `--` arguments")
        run = rename_main
    elif argv[:1] == ["archive-window"]:
        p = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="ade-worker-run archive-window")
        p.add_argument("--lead", required=True)
        p.add_argument("--window-middle")
        p.add_argument("--repo")
        p.add_argument("--placement", type=placement_arg, choices=("worker", "other"), default="worker",
                       help="which box to archive: the WORKER box (default) or the OTHER box")
        p.add_argument("--idle-handled", action="store_true")
        p.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
        p.add_argument("--on-behalf-of-lead", action="store_true")
        opts = p.parse_args(argv[1:])
        if rest:
            p.error("archive-window takes no `--` arguments")
        run = archive_window
    else:
        p = argparse.ArgumentParser(prog="ade-worker-run", description=__doc__.split("\n\n")[0])
        p.add_argument("--lead", required=True)
        p.add_argument("--slice", required=True)
        p.add_argument("--window-middle")
        p.add_argument("--repo")
        p.add_argument("--cwd", type=os.path.expanduser)  # a leading `~` is the caller's home even when no shell expanded it (--cwd=~/x, a quoted ~)
        p.add_argument("--no-footer", action="store_true")
        p.add_argument("--worktree", help="the worktree the worker writes in, named in its tab (`[wt: <dir>]`); a --cwd that is a "
                       "linked worktree is named without this")
        p.add_argument("--placement", type=placement_arg, choices=("worker", "lead", "other"), default="worker",
                       help="the box: worker (default, every worker and reviewer), lead (the lead's own window; alias main), "
                       "other (probes and side tasks)")
        p.add_argument("--interactive", action="store_const", const="lead", dest="placement",
                       help="alias for --placement lead: a worker the operator asked for interactively")
        p.add_argument("--other", action="store_const", const="other", dest="placement", help="alias for --placement other")
        p.add_argument("--on-behalf-of-lead", action="store_true")
        p.add_argument("--mcp", action="append", default=[], metavar="NAME",
                       help="give this worker the on-demand MCP server NAME (config/mcp-on-demand.toml; repeatable): the launch "
                       "uses the Paseo provider profile <provider>-mcp-NAME, docs/mcp-on-demand.md 11.2")
        opts = p.parse_args(argv)
        if opts.mcp:  # an unknown name or a bad registry is a usage error (exit 2) before anything is launched
            try:
                known = mcpod.load_registry()
            except mcpod.McpError as e:
                p.error(str(e))
            for n in opts.mcp:
                if n not in known:
                    p.error(f"unknown --mcp name {n!r}; known: {', '.join(sorted(known)) or 'none'}")
        run = lambda o: launch(o, rest)  # noqa: E731
    try:
        return run(opts)
    except Refused as e:
        sys.stderr.write(f"ade-worker-run: {e}\n")
        return 1


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))
